      "reasons": [
        "The requested field is not defensible here: a psychopharmacological drug is a medication/drug, not a diagnosis.",
        "The definition goes beyond the source by generalizing to “mental disorders” in general; the packet only says these drugs are frequently used in more severe cases of patients with mental disorders and in the context of comorbid cardiovascular disease.",
        "The phrase “usually tolerated” is broader than the packet, which says the drugs are generally well tolerated and efficacious but require consideration of drug- and dose-dependent side effects in this specific clinical context."
